# ELLE (Legacy Source Tree README)

This directory once contained its own Imake / install script based build system.
Those mechanisms (Imakefile, install.sh, install.win, config.guess/sub, Makefile, *.tmpl, extra.rules)
have been removed in favor of a unified Conan + CMake + Ninja workflow at the repository root.

## Current Build Instructions
See the top-level `BUILD.md` for authoritative, up-to-date build, install, and packaging steps.
Typical build (Release, headless):

```
conan install . -s build_type=Release --build=missing -of build
cmake -S . -B build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=build/conan_toolchain.cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
cmake --build build -j
```

Executables and libraries are written to the `build/` directory only; the source tree should remain clean.

## GUI (Optional)
If GUI support is reintroduced, it will be done through CMake options (e.g. `-DELLE_BUILD_GUI=ON`) once the
`wxWidgets` dependency is added to `conanfile.txt`. Historical WX build paths in this directory are deprecated.

## What Was Removed
- Legacy install scripts: `install.sh`, `install.win`
- Imake / X11 templates: `Imakefile`, `elle.tmpl`, `extra.rules`, `Makefile*`
- Autoconf triplet helpers: `config.guess`, `config.sub`
- Prebuilt static archives and object files (previous clean-up step)

These files offered no functionality beyond what the consolidated CMake project now provides and could cause confusion.

## Migration Notes
Historical notes about source adjustments and modernization are tracked in `PORTING_NOTES.md` and `CHANGELOG.md`.
If you need to reproduce an ancient environment, consult version control history prior to their removal.

## Contributing
See `CONTRIBUTING.md` at the repository root. Please avoid committing build outputs (`*.o`, legacy `lib*.a`, etc.); CI enforces a clean tree.

## License
Refer to the root `LICENSE`. Any legacy license texts in subfolders remain informational only.

